00:59:49.280 --> 00:59:51.360
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Ah, Ma'am Maria Ballesteros.

asr-001044
00:59:51.580 --> 00:59:53.100
Senator Erwin Tulfo: How long is your presentation, ma'am?

asr-001045
00:59:53.140 --> 00:59:54.660
Senator Erwin Tulfo: I only have few questions for you.

asr-001046
00:59:54.660 --> 00:59:55.960
Senator Erwin Tulfo: How long is your presentation?

asr-001047
00:59:57.920 --> 00:59:58.600
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Go ahead, po.

asr-001048
01:00:00.000 --> 01:00:14.980
CESB Executive Director Maria Marcy Cosare-Ballesteros: Thank you. Good afternoon, our distinguished budget sponsor, Honorable Senator Erwin Tulfo, to Chairperson of Civil Service Marilyn Barua Yap, Chairperson Urduja Alvarado.

asr-001049
01:00:14.980 --> 01:00:24.100
CESB Executive Director Maria Marcy Cosare-Ballesteros: Ladies and gentlemen, good afternoon. I am pleased to present the proposed budget of the Career Executive Service Board for fiscal year 2027.

asr-001050
01:00:24.100 --> 01:00:41.680
CESB Executive Director Maria Marcy Cosare-Ballesteros: Our proposed budget will support the CES Board in delivering and fulfilling its unique mandate enshrined in Presidential Decree No. 1 to promulgate rules, standard procedures in the selection, classification, compensation, and career development of the members of the CES.

asr-001051
01:00:42.240 --> 01:00:50.080
CESB Executive Director Maria Marcy Cosare-Ballesteros: It is noteworthy that our mandate covers the four pillars of the human resource management in the third level.

asr-001052
01:00:51.300 --> 01:00:56.800
CESB Executive Director Maria Marcy Cosare-Ballesteros: Our budget is aligned with the Philippine Development Plan 2023 to 2028.

asr-001053
01:00:56.800 --> 01:01:24.080
CESB Executive Director Maria Marcy Cosare-Ballesteros: Under Chapter 14, Outcome 4, where competent, motivated, resilient public servants are supported, it specifically provides that the CES system will be strengthened through merit and fitness, where the potential and qualified third-level officials will undergo the four-stage CES eligibility examination process, the CES leadership management proficiency program, and other lifelong learning programs for appointment to CES

asr-001054
01:01:24.100 --> 01:01:54.080
CESB Executive Director Maria Marcy Cosare-Ballesteros: rank to build up a critical mass of CES officers and eligibles. It complements our mission to infuse the bureaucracy with well-selected and development-oriented leaders, [unclear] bring change, expertise and leadership for responsive public service. Under our PREXC, the CESB operations is focused on the core program of career executive screening and development to ensure and promote merit and fitness for entry to the CES and sustaining a continuing pool of CES

asr-001055
01:01:54.100 --> 01:02:24.080
CESB Executive Director Maria Marcy Cosare-Ballesteros: eligibles and CESOs. Our proposed budget for 2027 in summary, originally we proposed 219 million but we were only provided with 142.857 million under the National Expenditure Program. Our 2027 budget per NEP consists only of personnel services

asr-001056
01:02:24.100 --> 01:02:58.300
CESB Executive Director Maria Marcy Cosare-Ballesteros: and MOOE without capital outlay. This NEP, our budget in the NEP, represents an increase of 34% from our previous 2026 budget due to the 58% increase in MOOE and 8% increase in personnel services. The 58% increase in MOOE for 2027 is mainly because of the issuance of the Permanent Committee Resolution 2026-01 issued in July 2026.

asr-001057
01:02:58.300 --> 01:03:24.080
CESB Executive Director Maria Marcy Cosare-Ballesteros: The Permanent Committee composed of the Secretary of the Budget and Management, Department of Finance Secretary and COA Chairperson, requiring the closure of the CESB revolving fund beginning 2027. The Permanent Committee granted limited authority to the CES Board to utilize fees collected from our examination and training activities through a revolving fund

asr-001058
01:03:24.100 --> 01:03:54.080
CESB Executive Director Maria Marcy Cosare-Ballesteros: until the end of 2026 only. Thus, we are required to close the CESB revolving fund account. Hence, the CESB was advised to include all its funding requirements for the 2027 budget under the GAA or the General Appropriations Act. The proposed increase in the MOOE will cover 31 million, 31.6 million in the NEP to cover the MOOE for the core program operations which were previously charged

asr-001059
01:03:54.100 --> 01:04:24.080
CESB Executive Director Maria Marcy Cosare-Ballesteros: to the revolving fund. It consists of eligibility examination process, appointment and promotion in CES rank, CES capacity building, CES performance management, recognition and executive placement. Consequently, in view of the Permanent Committee resolution, we are also proposing the inclusion of the phrase examinations, assessment, performance validation and panel interviews in Section 13 of the general appropriations,

asr-001060
01:04:24.100 --> 01:04:54.080
CESB Executive Director Maria Marcy Cosare-Ballesteros: general provisions of the 2027 GAA, as these items are not in the current GAA provision stipulations, to enable us to utilize the budget in the NEP for the implementation of our core programs. On top of the NEP, we are requesting for reconsideration of the Senate Committee on Finance for the approval of additional budget request of 66.917, 66.9 million.

asr-001061
01:04:54.100 --> 01:05:11.500
CESB Executive Director Maria Marcy Cosare-Ballesteros: This includes prioritized budget items under the original proposal amounting to 18.9 million consisting of re-fleeting of six motor vehicles classified as unserviceable and for replacement under the DBM circular, 2022-1.

asr-001061-split-2
01:05:11.500 --> 01:05:17.000
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Executive Director Ballesteros, hindi po nila sinama ba yan yung request ninyo ng transportation na yan?

asr-001061-split-3
01:05:17.000 --> 01:05:17.350
CESB Executive Director Maria Marcy Cosare-Ballesteros: Hindi po.

asr-001061-split-4
01:05:17.350 --> 01:05:18.200
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Magkano po yan?

asr-001061-split-5
01:05:18.200 --> 01:05:25.000
CESB Executive Director Maria Marcy Cosare-Ballesteros: 13 million, 13.251. We have been requesting this for four years already, sir.

asr-001062
01:05:25.000 --> 01:05:25.600
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Magkano po?

asr-001062-split-2
01:05:25.600 --> 01:05:31.660
CESB Executive Director Maria Marcy Cosare-Ballesteros: 13 million, 251,000.

asr-001062-split-3
01:05:31.660 --> 01:05:33.380
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Okay, I'll help you out. Go ahead.

asr-001062-split-4
01:05:33.380 --> 01:05:54.080
CESB Executive Director Maria Marcy Cosare-Ballesteros: Okay. So also some equipment for the approved new plantilla positions in our Eligibility and Rank Appointment Division, and also for the regular repairs and maintenance of our building and some professional services for management and monitoring inspection of the construction of the new CESB

asr-001063
01:05:54.100 --> 01:06:14.160
CESB Executive Director Maria Marcy Cosare-Ballesteros: building at UP Diliman under the budget of the DPWH. And we also request, Honorable Senator, the additional funding requirement for the total rehabilitation, rehabilitation of the electrical system and related structural repairs in our old CESB building.

asr-001063-split-2
01:06:14.160 --> 01:06:17.500
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Kasama na po ba diyan sa 66.9?

asr-001063-split-3
01:06:17.500 --> 01:06:18.500
CESB Executive Director Maria Marcy Cosare-Ballesteros: Yes po. Yes po.

asr-001063-split-4
01:06:18.500 --> 01:06:19.000
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Okay.

asr-001063-split-5
01:06:19.000 --> 01:06:24.900
CESB Executive Director Maria Marcy Cosare-Ballesteros: Sa ngayon po kasi hindi namin ma-occupy ang aming old building and we are renting a temporary space.

asr-001064
01:06:24.900 --> 01:06:27.350
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Sa House of Representatives, pinaprubahan po nila ito?

asr-001064-split-2
01:06:27.350 --> 01:06:28.000
CESB Executive Director Maria Marcy Cosare-Ballesteros: Yes po.

asr-001064-split-3
01:06:28.000 --> 01:06:28.600
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Alright.

asr-001064-split-4
01:06:28.600 --> 01:06:30.700
CESB Executive Director Maria Marcy Cosare-Ballesteros: Thank you so much po.

asr-001064-split-5
01:06:30.700 --> 01:06:31.650
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Okay.

asr-001064-split-6
01:06:31.650 --> 01:06:54.080
CESB Executive Director Maria Marcy Cosare-Ballesteros: So we have already requested the technical assistance of the Quezon City Government Engineering Department for the comprehensive rehabilitation plan of our electrical system and the repair works. This was not included in our original budget proposal as the emergency blackout incident happened after the deadline of submission of our budget to the DBM.

asr-001065
01:06:54.100 --> 01:07:24.080
CESB Executive Director Maria Marcy Cosare-Ballesteros: So these are just some slides. So, Honorable Sponsor, Senator Tulfo, we are therefore respectfully requesting the Senate Finance Committee's approval of our total proposed budget of 209.774 million consisting of the NEP and the additional 66.917 million for mission-critical priority budget items for

asr-001066
01:07:24.100 --> 01:07:54.080
CESB Executive Director Maria Marcy Cosare-Ballesteros: reconsideration of the Honorable Finance Committee. This will finance the priority programs of the CESB for FY 2027 consisting of career executive screening and development, namely eligibility examination process, appointment, promotion to CES rank, CES capacity building, professional development, performance management, recognition, executive placement and external relations of our career

asr-001067
01:07:54.100 --> 01:08:24.080
CESB Executive Director Maria Marcy Cosare-Ballesteros: executives; the formulation, implementation, monitoring of policies, regulations, ruling, legal opinions on the concerns of our CES officials; and general administration, support to operations including information systems development. Next slide. So this program will finance the four-stage CES eligibility process. We will, with this budget, we will be

asr-001068
01:08:24.100 --> 01:08:54.080
CESB Executive Director Maria Marcy Cosare-Ballesteros: able to serve our nationwide clients. We have a total of applicants for eligibility of 5,742, where 3,702 has already passed the CES written exam. We have also processed the assessment of 2,278 AC applicants and they are now moving towards the panel validation and panel interview for conferment of CES eligibility. We hope also to be

asr-001069
01:08:54.100 --> 01:09:24.080
CESB Executive Director Maria Marcy Cosare-Ballesteros: proactive in reaching out to the 1,319 incumbents of CES positions to assist them in their CES eligibility process. To show the size of the CES community we are serving, as of June 2026 we have in our roster 3,569 total active CESOs and CES eligibles. CESB caters to their needs as they participate in our lifelong learning programs, performance evaluation system conducted semestrally and executive placement on demand.

asr-001070
01:09:24.100 --> 01:09:33.680
CESB Executive Director Maria Marcy Cosare-Ballesteros: The next, the subsequent slides will also show the details of our physical target per core program. I will not anymore go through it one by one.

asr-001070-split-2
01:09:33.680 --> 01:09:54.080
Senator Erwin Tulfo: You don't need to. I'm okay with that and I can see, I, I only have a couple of questions for you. With the closure of CESB revolving fund pursuant to Permanent Committee Resolution No. 2026-01 dated July 16, 2026, can CESB explain the

asr-001071
01:09:54.100 --> 01:10:00.640
Senator Erwin Tulfo: financial, operational rationale or rationale for this closure? Magkano po ang remaining balance ng fund?

asr-001071-split-2
01:10:00.640 --> 01:10:06.440
CESB Executive Director Maria Marcy Cosare-Ballesteros: The remaining balance of the fund is 66. So if we are going to use the, the...

asr-001071-split-3
01:10:06.440 --> 01:10:11.880
Senator Erwin Tulfo: So this is what you're saying, the 66 na kuwan baka pwedeng idagdag doon sa nire-request.

asr-001071-split-4
01:10:11.880 --> 01:10:23.560
CESB Executive Director Maria Marcy Cosare-Ballesteros: Pero we are, we are using already in the conduct of our activities some of these funds, but by the end of the year we are going to return this to the national treasury. That's why

