Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: spend for marketing?

asr-002163
01:59:27.650 --> 01:59:28.300
DOT Assistant Secretary Armand Lorenze V. Sapitan: Yes, Sir.

asr-002164
01:59:28.300 --> 01:59:30.180
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Bawa, alam ko yung mga Malaysia,

asr-002165
01:59:30.180 --> 01:59:31.880
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: truly Asia, talagang matindi ang

asr-002166
01:59:31.880 --> 01:59:32.320
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: ano nun.

asr-002166-split-2
01:59:32.320 --> 01:59:32.920
DOT Assistant Secretary Armand Lorenze V. Sapitan: Yes, Sir.

asr-002166-split-3
01:59:32.920 --> 01:59:33.650
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Gastos dun.

asr-002167
01:59:33.650 --> 01:59:35.000
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Singapore.

asr-002168
01:59:35.000 --> 01:59:35.750
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Sorry, Sir.

asr-002169
01:59:35.750 --> 01:59:37.800
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So that we'll have an idea

asr-002170
01:59:37.800 --> 01:59:39.700
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: on the comparison.

asr-002171
01:59:39.700 --> 01:59:42.100
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Ayan yung branding budget.

asr-002172
01:59:42.100 --> 01:59:44.180
DOT Assistant Secretary Armand Lorenze V. Sapitan: Yeah, so for ang number one po

asr-002173
01:59:44.180 --> 01:59:46.180
DOT Assistant Secretary Armand Lorenze V. Sapitan: in terms of budget is Thailand

asr-002174
01:59:46.180 --> 01:59:48.180
DOT Assistant Secretary Armand Lorenze V. Sapitan: with 499 million.

asr-002175
01:59:48.180 --> 01:59:50.180
DOT Assistant Secretary Armand Lorenze V. Sapitan: This is in US dollars.

asr-002176
01:59:50.180 --> 01:59:51.180
DOT Assistant Secretary Armand Lorenze V. Sapitan: Followed by Singapore

asr-002177
01:59:51.180 --> 01:59:53.180
DOT Assistant Secretary Armand Lorenze V. Sapitan: with 418 million US dollars.

asr-002178
01:59:53.180 --> 01:59:55.180
DOT Assistant Secretary Armand Lorenze V. Sapitan: And then Malaysia, 331.

asr-002179
01:59:55.180 --> 01:59:56.180
DOT Assistant Secretary Armand Lorenze V. Sapitan: And number four po tayo,

asr-002180
01:59:56.180 --> 01:59:58.180
DOT Assistant Secretary Armand Lorenze V. Sapitan: 86.68 million.

asr-002181
01:59:58.180 --> 01:59:59.180
DOT Assistant Secretary Armand Lorenze V. Sapitan: But...

asr-002182
02:00:00.000 --> 02:00:09.340
DOT Assistant Secretary Armand Lorenze V. Sapitan: Kung makikita niyo po, sir, yung arrivals natin is mataas po versus Singapore, for example, and Thailand.

asr-002183
02:00:09.940 --> 02:00:18.100
DOT Assistant Secretary Armand Lorenze V. Sapitan: So for every 1 million US dollars that we invest in marketing, we get 74,758 tourists or travelers.

asr-002184
02:00:18.740 --> 02:00:22.000
DOT Assistant Secretary Armand Lorenze V. Sapitan: Ngayon po, yung Vietnam, if you will see, sir, it's an anomaly, sir.

asr-002185
02:00:22.000 --> 02:00:30.920
DOT Assistant Secretary Armand Lorenze V. Sapitan: Because it's the private sector po talaga yung nagdadrive ng kanilang tourism in terms of investments and promotions.

asr-002186
02:00:32.120 --> 02:00:41.400
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So what's the proposal of the agency now for the budget for branding?

asr-002187
02:00:41.760 --> 02:00:47.040
DOT Assistant Secretary Armand Lorenze V. Sapitan: So for 2027, sir, we are proposing 1 billion for branding and promotions alone.

asr-002188
02:00:48.880 --> 02:00:51.060
DOT Assistant Secretary Armand Lorenze V. Sapitan: And I can give you the breakdown, sir.

asr-002189
02:00:52.000 --> 02:00:57.620
DOT Assistant Secretary Armand Lorenze V. Sapitan: Yeah, so I mentioned earlier that we are in the middle of bidding out our media agencies.

asr-002190
02:00:57.780 --> 02:01:09.680
DOT Assistant Secretary Armand Lorenze V. Sapitan: So next year, once this is awarded, we will bid out another media agency to extend or to supplement the current efforts of the Refresh Love the Philippines campaign.

asr-002191
02:01:10.260 --> 02:01:16.620
DOT Assistant Secretary Armand Lorenze V. Sapitan: We are allocating 200 million pesos for that, followed by partnerships and co-branding activations.

asr-002192
02:01:17.440 --> 02:01:19.260
DOT Assistant Secretary Armand Lorenze V. Sapitan: Ito po yung partnership natin with the private sector.

asr-002193
02:01:20.300 --> 02:01:21.620
DOT Assistant Secretary Armand Lorenze V. Sapitan: So for example, yung club companies.

asr-002194
02:01:22.000 --> 02:01:32.120
DOT Assistant Secretary Armand Lorenze V. Sapitan: So co-branding with PAL or from other markets, local markets po, such as, for example, sa Korea, where we are doing interventions, yung mga local tour operators po nila.

asr-002195
02:01:32.820 --> 02:01:39.300
DOT Assistant Secretary Armand Lorenze V. Sapitan: And then we are also allocating 25 million for campaign monitoring, analytics, reporting, and social listening.

asr-002196
02:01:39.520 --> 02:01:51.520
DOT Assistant Secretary Armand Lorenze V. Sapitan: So right now, sir, ito po yung budget that we are allocating so that we get the social sentiment online or even, and parang be informed.

asr-002197
02:01:52.000 --> 02:01:59.940
DOT Assistant Secretary Armand Lorenze V. Sapitan: So if what, be informed of the campaigns that we are putting out there and whether they're working or not.

asr-002198
02:02:00.440 --> 02:02:04.440
DOT Assistant Secretary Armand Lorenze V. Sapitan: And then we're also allocating 25 million for brand health tracker.

asr-002199
02:02:04.440 --> 02:02:11.220
DOT Assistant Secretary Armand Lorenze V. Sapitan: So this is naman po what will diagnose basically the Refresh Love the Philippines campaign.

asr-002200
02:02:11.480 --> 02:02:21.440
DOT Assistant Secretary Armand Lorenze V. Sapitan: So what we'll do is we are creating like a brand metrics agency such as Kantar Nielsen.

asr-002201
02:02:22.000 --> 02:02:22.900
DOT Assistant Secretary Armand Lorenze V. Sapitan: So we're bidding it out.

asr-002202
02:02:23.580 --> 02:02:34.840
DOT Assistant Secretary Armand Lorenze V. Sapitan: We will do an analysis or diagnosis of, we will have them diagnose our, the pre-launch of the Refresh Love the Philippines.

asr-002203
02:02:34.980 --> 02:02:37.340
DOT Assistant Secretary Armand Lorenze V. Sapitan: So this is the social, the current state that we are in.

asr-002204
02:02:37.680 --> 02:02:45.800
DOT Assistant Secretary Armand Lorenze V. Sapitan: And then once we launch, ano po natin, the reception of the markets, target markets abroad, key markets and emerging markets.

asr-002205
02:02:46.040 --> 02:02:48.480
DOT Assistant Secretary Armand Lorenze V. Sapitan: And then six months after, ano po yung naging resulta nito?

asr-002206
02:02:48.980 --> 02:02:51.980
DOT Assistant Secretary Armand Lorenze V. Sapitan: Tumaas ba ang public sentiment towards the Philippines?

asr-002207
02:02:52.000 --> 02:02:54.540
DOT Assistant Secretary Armand Lorenze V. Sapitan: So yun po yung sa brand health tracker.

asr-002208
02:02:54.540 --> 02:03:00.000
DOT Assistant Secretary Armand Lorenze V. Sapitan: And then we are allocating 100 million for sub-brand and global media campaign.

asr-002209
02:03:00.320 --> 02:03:06.600
DOT Assistant Secretary Armand Lorenze V. Sapitan: So ito naman po yung, for, para po ito yung discover more to love natin.

asr-002210
02:03:06.600 --> 02:03:11.820
DOT Assistant Secretary Armand Lorenze V. Sapitan: So we are not replacing Love the Philippines, but rather we are coming up with like mga maliliit na sub-campaigns po.

asr-002211
02:03:11.880 --> 02:03:12.380
DOT Assistant Secretary Armand Lorenze V. Sapitan: So we are.

asr-002212
02:03:12.480 --> 02:03:17.500
Senator Erwin Tulfo: I have one quick question, if you would, si Chair, kay Secretary dito siguro.

asr-002213
02:03:18.640 --> 02:03:21.020
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Parang tayo lang ang bansa na paiba-iba.

asr-002214
02:03:21.300 --> 02:03:21.840
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Bawat administration.

asr-002216
02:03:22.000 --> 02:03:30.300
Senator Erwin Tulfo: May love, may more love, may love-love, may more fun, may wow, may wow Philippines, kung ano-ano.

asr-002217
02:03:30.460 --> 02:03:33.240
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Every time na may bagong administration, bakit ganun?

asr-002218
02:03:33.560 --> 02:03:37.580
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Wala tayong tatakman eh. Unlike Malaysia, truly Asia.

asr-002219
02:03:38.220 --> 02:03:39.280
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Ay mga ganun eh, diba?

asr-002220
02:03:39.820 --> 02:03:43.880
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Kaya mamaya-maya, pustahan tayo. Pag pumalitan ng administration, hindi na love yan.

asr-002221
02:03:44.220 --> 02:03:45.700
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Hate ba yan? Kung ano man yan.

asr-002222
02:03:46.160 --> 02:03:48.420
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Come to the Philippines, enjoy the Philippines.

asr-002223
02:03:49.140 --> 02:03:50.540
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Why do we change?

asr-002224
02:03:50.540 --> 02:04:09.720
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Parang I don't see anything wrong with wow Philippines, talagang dumami ho, tapos pinalitan, tapos papalitan, it's more fun ngayon, love, love the Philippines, baka next administration na ito, come to the Philippines, mamuhay ka sa Philippines, what is going on in here?

asr-002225
02:04:10.180 --> 02:04:17.040
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: Yes sir, I totally agree with you because we should not have really kept on changing the tagline po.

asr-002226
02:04:17.040 --> 02:04:20.460
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: So ang una ko pong ginawa, nung dumating,

asr-002227
02:04:20.540 --> 02:04:25.440
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: Ako, love the Philippines, I will preserve love the Philippines po.

asr-002228
02:04:25.740 --> 02:04:29.360
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: So kung makikita niyo po lahat ng campaign namin, it's love the Philippines.

asr-002229
02:04:29.720 --> 02:04:39.020
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: May konting, depending po anong campaign, anong season o anong target market ang inaanon namin, nagkaroon ng discover more to love.

asr-002230
02:04:39.180 --> 02:04:43.220
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: But that still emanates from the organic love the Philippines.

asr-002231
02:04:43.440 --> 02:04:44.940
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: Bakit po discover more to love?

asr-002232
02:04:44.940 --> 02:04:47.920
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: Kasi po, nung dumating kami, ako po,

asr-002233
02:04:47.920 --> 02:04:54.920
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: yung ano, there's a very sharp drop in that sentiment for travel, plus mahal pa tayo.

asr-002234
02:04:55.480 --> 02:05:02.340
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: So sabi ko, instead of our tourism assets becoming stranded, let's launch a domestic tourism campaign.

asr-002235
02:05:02.880 --> 02:05:04.200
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: And that's what we actually did.

asr-002236
02:05:04.600 --> 02:05:09.300
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: So pag love the Philippines, sa kababayan po natin, baka nakatira dito,

asr-002237
02:05:09.840 --> 02:05:13.400
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: discover more to love because we are highlighting the hidden gems.

asr-002238
02:05:13.400 --> 02:05:17.300
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: Hindi lang yung nakita nyo, hindi lang yung alam nyo, marami po pa yan.

asr-002239
02:05:17.300 --> 02:05:19.740
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: So it's still under the love the Philippines.

asr-002240
02:05:19.820 --> 02:05:22.140
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: At hindi nilang po discover Philippines. Parang ganun.

asr-002241
02:05:22.260 --> 02:05:29.600
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Or my next question, Secretary, do we, must we pass a law para hindi po bago-baguhin nila ito?

asr-002242
02:05:30.000 --> 02:05:31.360
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Parang pinaglalaruan.

asr-002243
02:05:31.940 --> 02:05:38.480
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Pag ako nung naisip ng bagong appoint na Secretary, palitan ko kaya ito dahil hindi ko gusto.

asr-002244
02:05:39.020 --> 02:05:41.080
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Yung nakaraang Secretary may credit nito.

asr-002245
02:05:41.080 --> 02:05:47.260
Senator Erwin Tulfo: So sabihin, yung susunod na DOT Secretary, itong love ni Secretary Mata, hindi ko gusto ito eh.

asr-002246
02:05:47.300 --> 02:05:50.440
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Siya ang naalala ng mga tao, dapat meron akong sarili.

asr-002247
02:05:50.960 --> 02:05:54.180
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Every administration, meron tayong bago.

asr-002248
02:05:54.540 --> 02:05:56.580
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Why don't we stick? Kailangan ba ng batas?

asr-002249
02:05:56.680 --> 02:06:02.500
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Kasi kung kailangan ma'am, then we'll have to file a law na huwag nyo na pakialaman niyang branding natin.

asr-002250
02:06:02.620 --> 02:06:03.480
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Kasi paiba-iba eh.

asr-002251
02:06:04.420 --> 02:06:08.160
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: Right on the bat sir, kung pwede po, i-legislate na natin yun.

asr-002252
02:06:08.620 --> 02:06:11.040
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: Kasi anyway, maganda naman yung love the Philippines.

asr-002253
02:06:11.040 --> 02:06:15.940
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: Kasi ang ating asset po sir, is the people are the best asset.

asr-002254
02:06:16.100 --> 02:06:17.240
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: And there's a lot of things.

asr-002255
02:06:17.400 --> 02:06:20.280
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: From our caregivers overseas, from our seaman too.

asr-002256
02:06:20.640 --> 02:06:21.680
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: And then we have more here.

asr-002257
02:06:21.780 --> 02:06:28.460
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: Kasi ang hospitality ng Pilipino po, at saka ang lambing, hindi mo papantayan sa ASEAN o kahit sa ibang lugar.

asr-002258
02:06:28.940 --> 02:06:34.000
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: So if we can legislate and we use love the Philippines, I think I'm all for it sir.

asr-002259
02:06:35.820 --> 02:06:38.780
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: I agree with the concern of our chair.

asr-002260
02:06:38.780 --> 02:06:43.280
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: I think we should really stick with one branding.

asr-002261
02:06:43.760 --> 02:06:46.620
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Kasi pagpaiba-iba, yun ang problema sa Pilipinas eh.

asr-002262
02:06:47.300 --> 02:06:51.340
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Ano yung pag may change of administration, pinapalitan din lahat.

asr-002263
02:06:51.820 --> 02:06:57.780
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Kaya nga, binpushing ni sir chair yung comprehensive, yung master plan for infrastructure and national development.

asr-002264
02:06:58.020 --> 02:06:59.940
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Pero dapat kasama na rin ito sa tourism.

asr-002265
02:07:00.660 --> 02:07:05.740
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: At least we will have our, yung recall kasi it's difficult to achieve.

asr-002266
02:07:05.740 --> 02:07:08.820
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: It takes years or decades.

asr-002267
02:07:09.440 --> 02:07:11.420
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Kaya nga yung Malaysia through Asia, talagang yun lang.

asr-002268
02:07:12.060 --> 02:07:12.660
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Nagsistake.

asr-002269
02:07:12.780 --> 02:07:16.740
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So I'm hoping that we will this time, we will stick.

asr-002270
02:07:17.300 --> 02:07:17.800
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: To it, no?

asr-002271
02:07:18.000 --> 02:07:25.100
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Kasi siguro from, it's more from the Philippines, tapos nag-love the Philippines, rebranding tayo.

asr-002272
02:07:25.220 --> 02:07:29.740
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: That takes a lot of effort and expense also.

asr-002273
02:07:29.980 --> 02:07:32.980
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Dapat nga nag-double tayo kasi rebranding yun eh, no?

asr-002274
02:07:33.400 --> 02:07:35.480
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So I'm hoping that tama naman yung ano.

asr-002275
02:07:35.480 --> 02:07:39.360
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: I agree with the chair that we really have to stick to one.

asr-002276
02:07:39.780 --> 02:07:45.340
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So para in that way, we have yung recall, no?

asr-002277
02:07:45.420 --> 02:07:46.480
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: That's difficult to...

asr-002278
02:07:47.300 --> 02:07:48.060
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: To attain.

asr-002279
02:07:48.440 --> 02:07:50.520
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Si Mr. Chair, ang ano ko lang natin, no?

asr-002280
02:07:50.820 --> 02:07:58.900
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: With the short presentation, although admittedly, we're only the fourth in terms of spending,

asr-002281
02:07:58.900 --> 02:08:02.900
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: in terms of tourism promotions internationally.

asr-002282
02:08:03.860 --> 02:08:08.280
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Pero sa tourism arrivals, doon tayo naka, doon yun ang nakakalungkot, no?

asr-002283
02:08:08.360 --> 02:08:10.360
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: We are one of the last, no?

asr-002284
02:08:11.040 --> 02:08:12.080
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Sa ASEAN countries.

asr-002285
02:08:12.520 --> 02:08:17.140
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Well, of course, Vietnam, kakasabi nyo lang, because of the private efforts, kakaiba, no?

asr-002286
02:08:17.300 --> 02:08:18.880
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Everyone's going to Vietnam now.

asr-002287
02:08:20.900 --> 02:08:30.000
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: 5.95 million visitors in 2025 compared to 14.35 million ng Indonesia pa ito.

asr-002288
02:08:30.120 --> 02:08:34.140
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: And 17 million in Vietnam and Thailand, malaki rin.

asr-002289
02:08:34.140 --> 02:08:37.160
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So, what, ano?

asr-002290
02:08:38.420 --> 02:08:44.920
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: In our present monitoring by DOT ng tourist arrivals, did we improve this year?

asr-002291
02:08:45.380 --> 02:08:46.920
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Ano po ang present, ano, natin?

asr-002292
02:08:47.300 --> 02:08:48.500
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: Yes, sir.

asr-002293
02:08:48.820 --> 02:08:54.700
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: As of August 2026, we have recorded 4.11 million foreign visitors na po.

asr-002294
02:08:55.060 --> 02:08:58.020
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: It's up 3.7% from last year.

asr-002295
02:08:58.700 --> 02:09:03.820
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: Our target po sana is 6.4 at the low end, 6.8 at the high end po.

asr-002296
02:09:04.920 --> 02:09:11.000
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: So, while we are growing, we recognize po that we need to accelerate that growth in the remaining months po.

asr-002297
02:09:11.000 --> 02:09:17.000
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: So, beyond spending for promotion, we would like to address the entire change.

asr-002298
02:09:17.300 --> 02:09:23.860
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: First, air connectivity, kasi 99% of all travels to our country is by air.

asr-002299
02:09:24.420 --> 02:09:31.720
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: So, from January to May 19 po, we already recorded 7.78 million international seats.

asr-002300
02:09:31.920 --> 02:09:34.860
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: It's 8.31% year-on-year increase.

asr-002301
02:09:35.180 --> 02:09:45.300
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: So, we are continuing to work with the airlines, the air operators, DOTR, to add routes and frequencies, particularly po sa secondary gateways.

asr-002302
02:09:45.300 --> 02:09:47.220
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: For example po, China is good.

asr-002303
02:09:47.220 --> 02:09:52.960
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: For example, kasi we have added direct routes from Hangzhou, Changsha, and Chongqing.

asr-002304
02:09:53.420 --> 02:10:03.180
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: And ito po, from January to August, may kita niyo, tumaas po ang arrivals from China to 69.15%, about 310,000.

asr-002305
02:10:03.640 --> 02:10:08.360
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: Tapos po, ang next strategy namin is we are becoming more market-specific.

asr-002306
02:10:08.360 --> 02:10:15.380
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: Our largest markets from January to August was United States with 800,000 plus arrivals.

asr-002307
02:10:15.760 --> 02:10:16.860
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: South Korea, second.

asr-002308
02:10:17.220 --> 02:10:19.360
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: With 700,000 plus arrivals.

asr-002309
02:10:19.540 --> 02:10:22.060
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: And Japan with 350,000 and China.

asr-002310
02:10:22.540 --> 02:10:24.920
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: Australia po is 234,000.

asr-002311
02:10:25.140 --> 02:10:28.320
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: So, these markets do not behave the same way.

asr-002312
02:10:28.660 --> 02:10:33.360
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: So, our airline partnerships and tourism products will be tailored accordingly.

asr-002313
02:10:33.920 --> 02:10:36.540
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: Thirdly po, we are making the Philippines easier to visit.

asr-002314
02:10:36.680 --> 02:10:43.400
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: So, we are working po with DFA and other agencies para po matanggal yung friction, like visa entry facilitation.

asr-002315
02:10:43.960 --> 02:10:46.440
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: Tapos, fourth, we are focusing po on value.

asr-002316
02:10:47.220 --> 02:10:54.400
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: So, we want our visitors po to stay longer and spend more, travel beyond the major gateways.

asr-002317
02:10:54.760 --> 02:10:58.220
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: And finally po, we are using tourism to attract investment.

asr-002318
02:10:58.440 --> 02:11:08.120
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: TESA has already registered 14.5 billion in tourism investments across 34 projects under CREATE since 2021,

asr-002319
02:11:08.460 --> 02:11:13.840
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: with 10 billion coming in 2020 through August 2026 alone.

asr-002320
02:11:14.260 --> 02:11:17.140
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: At the same time po, just lumabas lang kahapon sa news.

asr-002321
02:11:17.220 --> 02:11:29.840
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: The hotel sector reported a pipeline of approximately 387 billion in investments for 45,884 new hotel rooms across 213 projects.

asr-002322
02:11:30.200 --> 02:11:38.240
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: So, we will continue po to market the Philippines, but we will also make it easier to reach and make it more accessible to move around.

asr-002323
02:11:38.900 --> 02:11:40.200
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: That's it, sir. Thank you.

asr-002324
02:11:41.660 --> 02:11:43.620
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Well, we know the challenges, no?

asr-002325
02:11:43.620 --> 02:11:45.680
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: As you mentioned, we are an archipelago.

asr-002326
02:11:47.220 --> 02:11:49.100
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Land, lahat sila, by land, no?

asr-002327
02:11:49.160 --> 02:11:51.200
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Karamihan, kaya mas marami.

asr-002328
02:11:51.360 --> 02:11:58.620
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Challenges, challenge talaga because by air, most of our arrivals, and marami din tayong challenge na kailangan nating ayusin.

asr-002329
02:11:58.840 --> 02:12:03.000
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Well, of course, our airports, for one, has to be more friendlier.

asr-002330
02:12:03.120 --> 02:12:08.620
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: And I think, na iya naman is trying to, the new na iya management is trying to fix that, no?

asr-002331
02:12:08.880 --> 02:12:15.800
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: In fact, in the other day, nung nagkaroon ng DOJ sa immigration natin, we also asked them, no?

asr-002332
02:12:15.840 --> 02:12:16.620
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Kasi there are several...

asr-002333
02:12:17.220 --> 02:12:21.900
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: It's that they're installed, pero ang nakakagamit lang, napansin nga ni Senator Tulpo yun eh.

asr-002334
02:12:22.500 --> 02:12:33.120
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Bakit pag-arrival, ang nakakagamit lang, Pilipino, foreigners have to go through the usual immigration officers, no?

asr-002335
02:12:33.700 --> 02:12:38.460
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Pag naman doon sa departure, ang foreigner lang ang pwede, ang Pilipino, hindi.

asr-002336
02:12:38.640 --> 02:12:39.780
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Kailangan din sila, ano.

asr-002337
02:12:39.780 --> 02:12:45.000
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: But they already presented that it's, magkakaroon sila ng gradual facing.

asr-002338
02:12:45.740 --> 02:12:47.180
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So, dahan-dahan.

asr-002339
02:12:47.220 --> 02:12:51.740
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: They will be allowing already the use of e-gates more, no?

asr-002340
02:12:51.860 --> 02:12:52.980
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Para ma-utilize.

asr-002341
02:12:53.520 --> 02:12:55.240
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So, yun, convenience din kasi yun eh.

asr-002342
02:12:55.360 --> 02:12:55.520
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Diba?

asr-002343
02:12:55.620 --> 02:13:00.880
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: I think, the seat part, ano, the seat, ano, malaking, I'm sure, Secretary, this is a big, ano, no?

asr-002344
02:13:01.420 --> 02:13:04.320
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Big factor din po yung convenience, saka yung connectivity natin.

asr-002345
02:13:05.000 --> 02:13:08.240
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Pupunta ka lang sa ibang terminal, parang mahirap sa atin eh.

asr-002346
02:13:08.560 --> 02:13:10.540
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: And also, yung transit.

asr-002347
02:13:10.700 --> 02:13:12.620
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So, there's a lot of challenges, we understand.

asr-002348
02:13:13.120 --> 02:13:14.380
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: But, what else?

asr-002349
02:13:14.900 --> 02:13:16.300
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: What else aside from promotion?

asr-002350
02:13:16.540 --> 02:13:16.920
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: What else?

asr-002351
02:13:16.920 --> 02:13:23.540
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: What other programs are you, are you doing to help increase our tourism?

asr-002352
02:13:23.840 --> 02:13:29.800
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Ang isang, yung nag-usapan namin ni Senator Tulfo, meron na ba tayong assessment nung competitiveness assessment?

asr-002353
02:13:29.980 --> 02:13:41.900
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Why is it that, why is it that our, our, some, some things like hotel, accommodation, hotels, restaurants sometimes are more expensive

asr-002354
02:13:41.900 --> 02:13:45.540
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: kung sa Thailand, saka sa mga Vietnam, are cheaper, no?

asr-002355
02:13:45.540 --> 02:13:46.240
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Yung mga hotels.

asr-002356
02:13:46.920 --> 02:13:48.400
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So, ano ba ang difference?

asr-002357
02:13:48.560 --> 02:13:52.240
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: And, what are we doing about this?

asr-002358
02:13:52.540 --> 02:13:57.780
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: And, saka siguro, alam nyo naman yung nag-viral, yung pampanong 1,600, no?

asr-002359
02:13:58.000 --> 02:13:58.520
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Sa Bohol.

asr-002360
02:13:58.600 --> 02:14:01.020
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Bohol is such a beautiful province.

asr-002361
02:14:01.200 --> 02:14:08.680
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: It's one of my favorite provinces na, unfortunately, their tourism arrivals also were affected this time.

asr-002362
02:14:08.680 --> 02:14:10.220
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So, are we looking at this?

asr-002363
02:14:11.000 --> 02:14:16.680
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Yung prices of our accommodation, yung hotels, prices of the...

asr-002364
02:14:16.920 --> 02:14:18.220
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: of food, no?

asr-002365
02:14:18.360 --> 02:14:19.700
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Yung nangyari dito, no?

asr-002366
02:14:19.780 --> 02:14:21.420
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Sana hindi na maulit-ulit yun, no?

asr-002367
02:14:21.420 --> 02:14:24.620
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: I think even the provincial government has stepped in.

asr-002368
02:14:24.740 --> 02:14:27.800
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So, siguro, in a nutshell, I know lots of challenges.

asr-002369
02:14:27.980 --> 02:14:33.880
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Siguro, Secdita, what, what, what else are we doing so that we can improve our arrivals?

asr-002370
02:14:34.560 --> 02:14:35.020
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: Okay, sir.

asr-002371
02:14:35.200 --> 02:14:44.360
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: Again, sir, we would like to highlight those other products na alam naming may pool, katulad po ng gastronomy, tourism po.

asr-002372
02:14:44.800 --> 02:14:46.360
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: Since we engaged Michelin.

asr-002373
02:14:46.920 --> 02:14:54.000
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: Kasi po, dumaki po ang transaction, both volume and value among those that have been recognized by Michelin po.

asr-002374
02:14:54.320 --> 02:14:56.720
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: And then, you're correct, sir, about the restaurants.

asr-002375
02:14:57.060 --> 02:14:59.900
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: Kasi, we are more expensive.

asr-002376
02:15:00.000 --> 02:15:07.680
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: than other maybe Asian countries pagdating sa cost of food and services.

asr-002377
02:15:07.920 --> 02:15:11.580
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: Pero sa food poster, it's a, I think, logistical issue.

asr-002378
02:15:11.760 --> 02:15:15.820
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: It's, you know, we have to have better cold chain facility,

asr-002379
02:15:16.040 --> 02:15:21.780
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: better roads, et cetera, to transport the items and produce in real time.

asr-002380
02:15:21.780 --> 02:15:24.380
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: So I think that's something that we can work on together

asr-002381
02:15:24.380 --> 02:15:27.320
DOT Secretary Dita Angara-Mathay: with Department of Transportation and Agriculture.

asr-002382
02:15:30.000 --> 02:15:32.360
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Just quickly, Mr. Chair, with your permission,

asr-002383
02:15:33.100 --> 02:15:38.760
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: there's a proposal to scrap travel tax, to ease travel costs.

asr-002384
02:15:39.660 --> 02:15:45.960
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: But I just want to ask TESA if there are concrete revenue alternatives

asr-002385
02:15:45.960 --> 02:15:51.760
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: presented to ensure it doesn't keep asking Congress directly

asr-002386
02:15:51.760 --> 02:15:53.680
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: kasi mawawala yung sa inyo yan, ano?

asr-002387
02:15:54.180 --> 02:15:57.620
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Directly, kung mawawala ang travel tax, it will affect TESA,

asr-002388
02:15:57.800 --> 02:15:59.560
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: yung infrastructure din natin.

asr-002389
02:16:00.000 --> 02:16:01.400
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Will be affected.

asr-002390
02:16:02.520 --> 02:16:07.440
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Sige, si GM, Dr. Mark Labid.

asr-002391
02:16:07.760 --> 02:16:08.280
TIEZA COO Mark T. Lapid: Thank you po.

asr-002392
02:16:08.320 --> 02:16:09.760
TIEZA COO Mark T. Lapid: With the permission of our Secretary,

asr-002393
02:16:10.620 --> 02:16:13.300
TIEZA COO Mark T. Lapid: Honorable Chairman, pleasant afternoon.

asr-002394
02:16:13.900 --> 02:16:16.540
TIEZA COO Mark T. Lapid: Mr. Chair, yes, regarding the issue of travel tax,

asr-002395
02:16:16.760 --> 02:16:18.740
TIEZA COO Mark T. Lapid: definitely we will be deeply affected

asr-002396
02:16:18.740 --> 02:16:24.180
TIEZA COO Mark T. Lapid: because 94% to 95% of our operation is coming from travel tax.

asr-002397
02:16:24.280 --> 02:16:27.800
TIEZA COO Mark T. Lapid: As a matter of fact, for 2027, Mr. Chair,

asr-002398
02:16:27.940 --> 02:16:29.940
TIEZA COO Mark T. Lapid: we already, as early as March,

asr-002399
02:16:30.000 --> 02:16:34.440
TIEZA COO Mark T. Lapid: we already submitted our proposed budget to DBM

asr-002400
02:16:34.440 --> 02:16:37.780
TIEZA COO Mark T. Lapid: since there's already a pending abolition of travel tax.

asr-002401
02:16:38.280 --> 02:16:44.120
TIEZA COO Mark T. Lapid: But I think in June, Mr. Chair, we received a letter coming from DBM

asr-002402
02:16:44.120 --> 02:16:49.040
TIEZA COO Mark T. Lapid: stating that they gave us zero budget allocation in the NEP.

asr-002403
02:16:49.560 --> 02:16:54.540
TIEZA COO Mark T. Lapid: So with that, Mr. Chair, wala akong binigay na item sa amin

asr-002404
02:16:54.540 --> 02:16:56.680
TIEZA COO Mark T. Lapid: or zero budget ang binigay sa amin ng DBM.

asr-002405
02:16:56.680 --> 02:16:59.980
TIEZA COO Mark T. Lapid: So what we did, we immediately revert muna.

asr-002406
02:17:00.000 --> 02:17:04.380
TIEZA COO Mark T. Lapid: to our board and submitted our corporate operating budget

asr-002407
02:17:04.380 --> 02:17:07.280
TIEZA COO Mark T. Lapid: for 2027, Mr. Chair.

asr-002408
02:17:07.400 --> 02:17:09.860
TIEZA COO Mark T. Lapid: Because as I mentioned a while ago,

asr-002409
02:17:10.340 --> 02:17:15.380
TIEZA COO Mark T. Lapid: we are heavily relying on the collection of travel tax,

asr-002410
02:17:15.920 --> 02:17:20.360
TIEZA COO Mark T. Lapid: which is around 4.03 billion for the CHESA share.

asr-002411
02:17:20.820 --> 02:17:25.640
TIEZA COO Mark T. Lapid: And the half of that is going to CHED and NCCA, Mr. Chair.

asr-002412
02:17:25.880 --> 02:17:27.920
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: And the majority goes to CHESA.

asr-002413
02:17:27.920 --> 02:17:29.820
TIEZA COO Mark T. Lapid: 50% po goes to us, sir.

asr-002414
02:17:30.000 --> 02:17:31.140
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: 40% goes to...

asr-002415
02:17:31.140 --> 02:17:35.400
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: So on a nutshell, Mr. Chair, gusto natin may alamin ni Senator Tulfo,

asr-002416
02:17:35.520 --> 02:17:38.620
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: ano-ano ba yung mga projects that, of course, yung mga infrastructure projects,

asr-002417
02:17:39.160 --> 02:17:41.320
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: but what will, ano pa yung mga main?

asr-002418
02:17:41.440 --> 02:17:47.500
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Of course, yung mga, ano yan, di ba, yung mga lounge, mga comfort rooms.

asr-002419
02:17:47.580 --> 02:17:51.400
TIEZA COO Mark T. Lapid: Sir, not only that, yung mga vital projects po namin ngayon,

asr-002420
02:17:51.520 --> 02:17:55.320
TIEZA COO Mark T. Lapid: like yung water problem ng El Nido, we're addressing it.

asr-002421
02:17:55.380 --> 02:17:57.760
TIEZA COO Mark T. Lapid: Coron, we're the one who's doing the STP also.

asr-002422
02:17:58.320 --> 02:17:59.620
TIEZA COO Mark T. Lapid: The one in Baguio.

asr-002423
02:18:00.000 --> 02:18:01.120
TIEZA COO Mark T. Lapid: May rin po ang gumagawa.

asr-002424
02:18:01.260 --> 02:18:07.640
TIEZA COO Mark T. Lapid: And then we're also the one who's rehabilitating the 10 domestic airports that we have, Mr. Chair,

asr-002425
02:18:07.740 --> 02:18:09.620
TIEZA COO Mark T. Lapid: that was submitted to us by CAAP.

asr-002426
02:18:10.440 --> 02:18:11.840
TIEZA COO Mark T. Lapid: So we're rehabilitating.

asr-002427
02:18:11.860 --> 02:18:13.280
TIEZA COO Mark T. Lapid: Not to mention the hotels, di ba?

asr-002428
02:18:13.400 --> 02:18:16.420
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: That's how you are also operating.

asr-002429
02:18:16.900 --> 02:18:18.200
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Malapit tayong Banawe, no?

asr-002430
02:18:18.220 --> 02:18:18.600
TIEZA COO Mark T. Lapid: Yes, sir.

asr-002431
02:18:18.640 --> 02:18:24.160
TIEZA COO Mark T. Lapid: Banawe, including the rehabilitation of Club Intramuros Golf Course also, Mr. Chair.

asr-002432
02:18:24.860 --> 02:18:26.040
TIEZA COO Mark T. Lapid: Sambuanga Golf Course.

asr-002433
02:18:26.360 --> 02:18:28.600
TIEZA COO Mark T. Lapid: So ito po yung mga nasa pipeline namin.

asr-002434
02:18:29.040 --> 02:18:29.960
TIEZA COO Mark T. Lapid: Aside from the other projects,

asr-002435
02:18:30.000 --> 02:18:30.960
TIEZA COO Mark T. Lapid: like the Burham Park.

asr-002436
02:18:30.960 --> 02:18:32.280
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: How many hotels sa GM?

asr-002437
02:18:32.480 --> 02:18:36.000
TIEZA COO Mark T. Lapid: We have at least four, Mr. Chair, na hotels.

asr-002438
02:18:36.200 --> 02:18:37.360
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Ano to? Yung Mount Dada?

asr-002439
02:18:37.360 --> 02:18:37.760
TIEZA COO Mark T. Lapid: Mount Dada.

asr-002440
02:18:38.080 --> 02:18:39.480
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Mount Dada, Manawe.

asr-002441
02:18:39.860 --> 02:18:41.500
TIEZA COO Mark T. Lapid: Then Balikasag, Mr. Chair.

asr-002442
02:18:41.780 --> 02:18:45.840
TIEZA COO Mark T. Lapid: And then the other one is Gardens of Malasag, Mr. Chair.

asr-002443
02:18:46.120 --> 02:18:50.220
TIEZA COO Mark T. Lapid: So yan po yung mga areas namin na inaayos as of now.

asr-002444
02:18:50.460 --> 02:18:54.660
TIEZA COO Mark T. Lapid: But aside from this one, sir, we're also supporting the LGUs from other projects,

asr-002445
02:18:54.800 --> 02:18:59.580
TIEZA COO Mark T. Lapid: like as I mentioned a while ago, the rehabilitation of Burham Park sa Burakay,

asr-002446
02:19:00.000 --> 02:19:04.440
TIEZA COO Mark T. Lapid: pa rin po kami sa Siargao, we're also part on the rehabilitation.

asr-002447
02:19:05.200 --> 02:19:10.060
TIEZA COO Mark T. Lapid: So yun lang po ang amin na different tourist facilities ang aming binibuilt,

asr-002448
02:19:10.180 --> 02:19:15.140
TIEZA COO Mark T. Lapid: which is more on vertical, including on the PCSSD, on the dive tourism, Mr. Chair.

asr-002449
02:19:15.140 --> 02:19:20.580
TIEZA COO Mark T. Lapid: We're also providing the hyperbaric chamber sa mga different dive destinations po natin.

asr-002450
02:19:20.860 --> 02:19:24.320
TIEZA COO Mark T. Lapid: So these were all being funded by the travel tax, Mr. Chair.

asr-002451
02:19:24.680 --> 02:19:29.500
Senator Erwin Tulfo: So what is your request, Dr. Lapid?

asr-002452
02:19:30.000 --> 02:19:31.740
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Ano hong request ninyo?

asr-002453
02:19:31.920 --> 02:19:37.300
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Na po pwede ituloy muna hanggang December yung pagkukulek ng travel tax?

asr-002454
02:19:37.420 --> 02:19:41.900
TIEZA COO Mark T. Lapid: Sir, we humbly request to your honor, Mr. Chair,

asr-002455
02:19:41.980 --> 02:19:46.860
TIEZA COO Mark T. Lapid: baka pwede po munang magkaroon tayo ng transition period for the travel tax.

asr-002456
02:19:47.360 --> 02:19:51.500
TIEZA COO Mark T. Lapid: We don't object with any denotion of the abolishment, Mr. Chair,

asr-002457
02:19:51.600 --> 02:19:55.640
TIEZA COO Mark T. Lapid: but as of now, with the current fiscal situation, Mr. Chair,

asr-002458
02:19:55.940 --> 02:19:59.200
TIEZA COO Mark T. Lapid: medyo may hirapan ho ang ahensya namin, not only us,

asr-002459
02:20:00.000 --> 02:20:03.640
TIEZA COO Mark T. Lapid: the tourism industry, when it comes to the infrastructure support,

asr-002460
02:20:04.060 --> 02:20:08.780
TIEZA COO Mark T. Lapid: e baka magkaroon po, sir, ng konting consideration to expand it for the meantime.

asr-002461
02:20:09.280 --> 02:20:15.040
TIEZA COO Mark T. Lapid: Since for 2027, sir, we don't have any budget that was given to us.

asr-002462
02:20:15.480 --> 02:20:18.880
TIEZA COO Mark T. Lapid: So how are the obligated projects na ginagawa ho namin?

asr-002463
02:20:19.000 --> 02:20:20.740
TIEZA COO Mark T. Lapid: How are we going to continue and sustain?

asr-002464
02:20:21.260 --> 02:20:24.300
TIEZA COO Mark T. Lapid: Plus the other in our pipeline, paano ho yan, Mr. Chair,

asr-002465
02:20:24.300 --> 02:20:27.540
TIEZA COO Mark T. Lapid: which we're also asking DBM about that question.

asr-002466
02:20:28.040 --> 02:20:29.860
