asr-002880
02:37:33.580 --> 02:37:33.900
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Not yet?

asr-002881
02:37:34.280 --> 02:37:41.500
NPF Executive Director Leonila R. Fabul: Hopefully, within this year, we can ground break if we already finalize all the technical details.

asr-002882
02:37:42.120 --> 02:37:44.800
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Okay, kasi hinahanap ng anak ko, hindi ko rin ho alam eh.

asr-002883
02:37:44.920 --> 02:37:46.480
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Ginu-google ko, saan na ba ito?

asr-002884
02:37:46.940 --> 02:37:52.360
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Eh para kayong, para kayong sasakyan, palipat-lipat, ano, dapat meron tayong fixed na?

asr-002885
02:37:52.380 --> 02:37:54.620
NPF Executive Director Leonila R. Fabul: And we have our signage in small museums.

asr-002886
02:37:55.300 --> 02:37:57.120
Senator Erwin Tulfo: When I was in grade school, I love that place.

asr-002887
02:37:57.260 --> 02:37:57.900
Senator Erwin Tulfo: It's very nice.

asr-002888
02:37:57.900 --> 02:37:59.720
Senator Erwin Tulfo: It's educational.

asr-002889
02:38:00.140 --> 02:38:00.240
NPF Executive Director Leonila R. Fabul: Yes.

asr-002890
02:38:00.240 --> 02:38:01.100
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Tapos marami po mga students.

asr-002891
02:38:01.180 --> 02:38:01.700
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Studyante.

asr-002892
02:38:01.860 --> 02:38:02.000
NPF Executive Director Leonila R. Fabul: Yes.

asr-002893
02:38:02.540 --> 02:38:03.020
NPF Executive Director Leonila R. Fabul: Tama po.

asr-002894
02:38:03.260 --> 02:38:15.560
Senator Erwin Tulfo: So, ngayon ba, may mandato po kayo, di ba, under presidential decree to establish parks, recreation center, libraries, etc., etc.?

asr-002895
02:38:15.560 --> 02:38:16.240
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Research, yes.

asr-002896
02:38:16.380 --> 02:38:22.760
Senator Erwin Tulfo: How would you execute that mandate kung ang budget niyo lang para sa capital outlay, 1.5 million?

asr-002897
02:38:23.660 --> 02:38:30.460
NPF Executive Director Leonila R. Fabul: Actually, the budget we have is 73M, but if we are able to get the NEDA budget,

asr-002898
02:38:30.460 --> 02:38:30.940
Senator Erwin Tulfo: All right.

asr-002899
02:38:31.180 --> 02:38:39.560
NPF Executive Director Leonila R. Fabul: 2 billion, that was based on the 2021 study that was made, but probably by 2026, it would be much higher.

asr-002900
02:38:39.840 --> 02:38:45.060
NPF Executive Director Leonila R. Fabul: But we are looking at other PPP options and other financial opportunities.

asr-002901
02:38:45.860 --> 02:38:46.380
NPF Executive Director Leonila R. Fabul: Thank you, po.

asr-002902
02:38:46.620 --> 02:38:47.020
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Thank you.

asr-002903
02:38:47.100 --> 02:38:47.420
Senator Erwin Tulfo: All right.

asr-002904
02:38:47.960 --> 02:38:48.280
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Comsec?

asr-002905
02:38:49.100 --> 02:38:53.860
Committee Secretary: Next to present is the Tourism Infrastructure and Enterprise Zone Authority.

asr-002906
02:38:55.200 --> 02:38:57.940
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Dr. Lapid, how long is your presentation, sir?

asr-002907
02:38:57.940 --> 02:39:00.540
TIEZA COO Mark T. Lapid: Sir, if I may, if we can just submit the...

asr-002908
02:39:00.540 --> 02:39:01.820
TIEZA COO Mark T. Lapid: Or go directly to the budget.

asr-002909
02:39:01.880 --> 02:39:03.400
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Can you just go directly to the budget?

asr-002910
02:39:03.540 --> 02:39:11.460
Senator Erwin Tulfo: And I know you're having a headache right now because once we remove that travel tax, you really have a big headache.

asr-002911
02:39:11.920 --> 02:39:13.300
Senator Erwin Tulfo: So, please go ahead.

asr-002912
02:39:16.660 --> 02:39:30.700
TIEZA COO Mark T. Lapid: For 2027, under our corporate operating budget, Mr. Chair, we submitted, our board has approved the 7.731,676 billion.

asr-002913
02:39:30.700 --> 02:39:35.240
TIEZA COO Mark T. Lapid: Together with the CHED share and the NCCA share.

asr-002914
02:39:35.280 --> 02:39:49.120
TIEZA COO Mark T. Lapid: For the TIEZA share, Mr. Chair, our proposed budget is 4.038 billion, which is a breakdown to our travel tax collection, which is 3.6.

asr-002915
02:39:49.120 --> 02:39:56.440
TIEZA COO Mark T. Lapid: Our receipts from the entities of 202 million, fees and charges coming from our tourism enterprise zones, which is 4.9.

asr-002916
02:39:56.440 --> 02:40:01.000
TIEZA COO Mark T. Lapid: Concession fee from our Puraki Island Water Company, 54 million.

asr-002917
02:40:01.000 --> 02:40:04.480
TIEZA COO Mark T. Lapid: From our other business income, which is 3.74.

asr-002918
02:40:05.460 --> 02:40:08.280
TIEZA COO Mark T. Lapid: That's coming from Corregidor and Hyperbatic Chamber.

asr-002919
02:40:08.880 --> 02:40:12.520
TIEZA COO Mark T. Lapid: Our other sources of income is 44.71.

asr-002920
02:40:12.840 --> 02:40:16.500
TIEZA COO Mark T. Lapid: That's coming from our rent, from our facilities and properties.

asr-002921
02:40:16.500 --> 02:40:21.020
TIEZA COO Mark T. Lapid: And our regulatory office, which is 35.48 million.

asr-002922
02:40:22.480 --> 02:40:27.400
TIEZA COO Mark T. Lapid: And our personal services is 738 million.

asr-002923
02:40:27.560 --> 02:40:30.120
TIEZA COO Mark T. Lapid: Our MOE is 1.077 billion.

asr-002924
02:40:30.540 --> 02:40:33.620
TIEZA COO Mark T. Lapid: Our equipment outlays 53.43 million.

asr-002925
02:40:33.820 --> 02:40:41.900
TIEZA COO Mark T. Lapid: And our improv project for 2027 will be 2.17 billion pesos, Mr. Chair.

asr-002926
02:40:42.360 --> 02:40:46.000
TIEZA COO Mark T. Lapid: So that would be for our budget for 2027, Mr. Chair.

asr-002927
02:40:46.440 --> 02:40:48.480
Senator Erwin Tulfo: One question lang po.

asr-002928
02:40:48.680 --> 02:40:49.160
TIEZA COO Mark T. Lapid: Yes, sir.

asr-002929
02:40:50.400 --> 02:40:54.440
Senator Erwin Tulfo: According to the Commission on Audit Findings, sir, Dr. Lapid,

asr-002930
02:40:55.260 --> 02:41:00.500
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Your office was not able to effectively implement daw a significant number,

asr-002931
02:41:00.700 --> 02:41:04.360
Senator Erwin Tulfo: of locally funded projects, with a contract cost of 3.3 billion.

asr-002932
02:41:04.800 --> 02:41:06.100
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Ano na hong status nito?

asr-002933
02:41:06.280 --> 02:41:09.000
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Naibigay niyo na po ba? Nasagot niyo na ang TIEZA?

asr-002934
02:41:09.260 --> 02:41:10.340
Senator Erwin Tulfo: What's going on here?

asr-002935
02:41:11.120 --> 02:41:17.160
TIEZA COO Mark T. Lapid: Mr. Chair, ito pong 3.3 are part of the funding na natanggalan po ng pondo,

asr-002936
02:41:17.260 --> 02:41:20.380
TIEZA COO Mark T. Lapid: project na natanggalan ng funding during the pandemic, Mr. Chair.

asr-002937
02:41:20.380 --> 02:41:26.920
TIEZA COO Mark T. Lapid: Because kinuhanan po kami ng 12 billion na budget namin ng Department of Finance

asr-002938
02:41:26.920 --> 02:41:31.400
TIEZA COO Mark T. Lapid: para i- gawin po, pondohan yung Bayanihan [unclear] One.

asr-002939
02:41:31.620 --> 02:41:34.200
Senator Erwin Tulfo: So, this was taken from your budget, this 3.3.

asr-002940
02:41:34.460 --> 02:41:34.780
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Okay.

asr-002941
02:41:35.000 --> 02:41:37.000
Senator Erwin Tulfo: So, it wasn't your fault?

asr-002942
02:41:37.360 --> 02:41:38.100
TIEZA COO Mark T. Lapid: No, sir.

asr-002943
02:41:38.280 --> 02:41:40.440
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Have you explained this to Commission on Audit?

asr-002944
02:41:40.440 --> 02:41:40.760
TIEZA COO Mark T. Lapid: Yes, sir.

asr-002945
02:41:40.760 --> 02:41:41.220
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Do they know?

asr-002946
02:41:41.320 --> 02:41:41.920
TIEZA COO Mark T. Lapid: We did po.

asr-002947
02:41:42.080 --> 02:41:43.060
TIEZA COO Mark T. Lapid: We submitted, sir.

asr-002948
02:41:43.140 --> 02:41:45.340
Senator Erwin Tulfo: So, you've already satisfied their query?

asr-002949
02:41:45.800 --> 02:41:49.660
TIEZA COO Mark T. Lapid: Actually, sir, we already got unqualified opinion coming from them.

asr-002950
02:41:49.860 --> 02:41:51.940
TIEZA COO Mark T. Lapid: So, we submitted everything sa kanila po.

asr-002951
02:41:52.220 --> 02:41:54.000
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Very good. Thank you, Dr. Lapid.

asr-002952
02:41:54.120 --> 02:41:54.580
TIEZA COO Mark T. Lapid: Thank you, sir.

asr-002953
02:41:54.600 --> 02:41:54.860
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Comsec?

asr-002954
02:41:55.340 --> 02:41:59.040
Committee Secretary: Next to present their budget is the Philippine Retirement Authority.

asr-002955
02:42:00.540 --> 02:42:04.120
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: Good afternoon, Mr. Chair.

asr-002956
02:42:05.420 --> 02:42:10.640
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: I'm not going to last very long because we are not asking for money from the government.

asr-002957
02:42:11.120 --> 02:42:13.260
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: Instead, we're bringing money to the government.

asr-002958
02:42:13.680 --> 02:42:14.840
Senator Erwin Tulfo: That's good to hear.

asr-002959
02:42:16.580 --> 02:42:22.660
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: Just give me five minutes so I can bring up what we have done so far for the government.

asr-002960
02:42:23.240 --> 02:42:26.460
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: The mandate of PRA, Philippine Retirement Authority,

asr-002961
02:42:26.460 --> 02:42:30.460
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: is really aside from making the Philippines haven,

asr-002962
02:42:30.540 --> 02:42:32.140
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: and for foreign retirees,

asr-002963
02:42:32.540 --> 02:42:37.300
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: is to increase the foreign currency reserve of our country.

asr-002964
02:42:37.840 --> 02:42:41.060
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: And I think we have done that because so far, as of now,

asr-002965
02:42:41.540 --> 02:42:48.740
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: we have in our banks a total of 654 million U.S. dollars.

asr-002966
02:42:49.680 --> 02:42:56.100
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: And by the end of this year, we expect it to go beyond the 700 million mark.

asr-002967
02:42:56.220 --> 02:43:00.520
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: And I think that alone is proof that we have reached,

asr-002968
02:43:00.680 --> 02:43:01.240
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: our mandate.

asr-002969
02:43:01.720 --> 02:43:03.580
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: The other mandate, as I mentioned earlier,

asr-002970
02:43:03.720 --> 02:43:07.920
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: was to make the Philippines a haven for foreign retirees.

asr-002971
02:43:08.680 --> 02:43:11.780
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: We just received two back-to-back awards,

asr-002972
02:43:12.320 --> 02:43:13.780
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: international awards.

asr-002973
02:43:13.780 --> 02:43:19.700
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: First, last year, TripZilla, which is a very popular booking platform,

asr-002974
02:43:20.200 --> 02:43:25.880
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: declared that the Philippines is the best retirement destination in Asia.

asr-002975
02:43:26.600 --> 02:43:30.280
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: Early this year, a London-based agency called

asr-002976
02:43:30.540 --> 02:43:36.080
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: Expat Repatriation Index announced that the Philippines

asr-002977
02:43:36.080 --> 02:43:39.700
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: is the number one retirement destination in the world.

asr-002978
02:43:40.340 --> 02:43:44.380
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: Between the two, I have better respect for the second,

asr-002979
02:43:44.380 --> 02:43:51.700
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: because the conclusion of coming up with the number one retirement destination for the Philippines

asr-002980
02:43:51.700 --> 02:43:54.200
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: was based on a rating system.

asr-002981
02:43:54.200 --> 02:43:56.200
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: They had five categories.

asr-002982
02:43:56.200 --> 02:44:00.040
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: First category was accessibility of a retirement visa.

asr-002983
02:44:00.540 --> 02:44:03.840
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: And they assigned 20 points for each category.

asr-002984
02:44:03.840 --> 02:44:08.900
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: Twenty points for the accessibility of a retirement visa.

asr-002985
02:44:08.900 --> 02:44:13.440
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: Twenty points for natural beauty of the country.

asr-002986
02:44:13.440 --> 02:44:15.380
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: Third would be the cost of living.

asr-002987
02:44:15.380 --> 02:44:17.900
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: Four would be hospitality index.

asr-002988
02:44:17.900 --> 02:44:20.380
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: And the fifth would be healthcare.

asr-002989
02:44:20.640 --> 02:44:24.460
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: We did very well in the first category,

asr-002990
02:44:24.480 --> 02:44:29.680
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: which says so much about what the PRA has been doing.

asr-002991
02:44:29.680 --> 02:44:33.780
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: we got a total, a perfect score of 20 points

asr-002992
02:44:33.780 --> 02:44:36.720
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: for the first category, visa accessibility.

asr-002993
02:44:37.540 --> 02:44:40.120
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: We didn't do too well in the healthcare category.

asr-002994
02:44:40.900 --> 02:44:42.660
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: Thailand did better than us.

asr-002995
02:44:43.020 --> 02:44:45.080
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: But when they totaled the whole thing,

asr-002996
02:44:45.580 --> 02:44:48.240
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: we still ended up one point ahead of Thailand.

asr-002997
02:44:48.780 --> 02:44:53.520
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: That's why we became the number one destination for the world.

asr-002998
02:44:53.620 --> 02:44:54.960
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: Now, why is that important?

asr-002999
02:44:54.960 --> 02:44:59.960
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: The total, the global retirement in...

asr-003000
02:45:00.000 --> 02:45:01.920
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: industry is estimated

asr-003001
02:45:01.920 --> 02:45:03.220
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: to be valued at

asr-003002
02:45:03.220 --> 02:45:05.960
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: 70 trillion US dollars.

asr-003003
02:45:06.640 --> 02:45:07.900
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: Now, if we are the number

asr-003004
02:45:07.900 --> 02:45:09.940
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: one choice to be the retirement

asr-003005
02:45:09.940 --> 02:45:11.840
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: destination, then we can get

asr-003006
02:45:11.840 --> 02:45:13.540
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: a good chunk of that amount

asr-003007
02:45:13.540 --> 02:45:15.840
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: as long as we continue to

asr-003008
02:45:15.840 --> 02:45:17.780
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: do what we're doing now, promoting

asr-003009
02:45:17.780 --> 02:45:19.240
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: to different parts of the world.

asr-003010
02:45:19.520 --> 02:45:21.500
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Sir, let me just ask you this question.

asr-003011
02:45:21.800 --> 02:45:24.080
Senator Erwin Tulfo: What are the basis for these people

asr-003012
02:45:24.080 --> 02:45:26.060
Senator Erwin Tulfo: to decide

asr-003013
02:45:26.060 --> 02:45:28.040
Senator Erwin Tulfo: to retire in our country

asr-003014
02:45:28.040 --> 02:45:28.680
Senator Erwin Tulfo: as foreigners?

asr-003015
02:45:28.680 --> 02:45:33.600
Senator Erwin Tulfo: What do they base it on?

asr-003016
02:45:35.520 --> 02:45:36.800
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Is it economy?

asr-003017
02:45:37.240 --> 02:45:38.680
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Is it tourism infrastructure?

asr-003018
02:45:40.100 --> 02:45:40.680
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Is it safety?

asr-003019
02:45:42.640 --> 02:45:43.820
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Feeling safe na

asr-003020
02:45:44.540 --> 02:45:46.140
Senator Erwin Tulfo: They will not be harmed

asr-003021
02:45:46.140 --> 02:45:47.460
Senator Erwin Tulfo: while they're here in the country

asr-003022
02:45:47.460 --> 02:45:48.780
Senator Erwin Tulfo: as they grow old?

asr-003023
02:45:48.980 --> 02:45:49.760
Senator Erwin Tulfo: What is it?

asr-003024
02:45:49.940 --> 02:45:52.280
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Or is it our beautiful women?

asr-003025
02:45:53.340 --> 02:45:54.200
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: No, that's last.

asr-003026
02:45:55.660 --> 02:45:56.980
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: The beautiful women

asr-003027
02:45:56.980 --> 02:45:57.780
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: is being considered.

asr-003028
02:45:57.780 --> 02:45:59.980
Senator Erwin Tulfo: I mean, it might sound like a joke,

asr-003029
02:46:00.040 --> 02:46:02.260
Senator Erwin Tulfo: but what I'm saying, I'm proud of Filipinas.

asr-003030
02:46:02.400 --> 02:46:02.640
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: Yes.

asr-003031
02:46:02.820 --> 02:46:05.180
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Well, we have beautiful ladies.

asr-003032
02:46:05.760 --> 02:46:07.420
Senator Erwin Tulfo: That's why we always win

asr-003033
02:46:07.420 --> 02:46:09.300
Senator Erwin Tulfo: in the international beauty pageants.

asr-003034
02:46:09.380 --> 02:46:09.660
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: Yes.

asr-003035
02:46:09.800 --> 02:46:11.380
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Because we have beautiful women.

asr-003036
02:46:11.940 --> 02:46:12.280
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: Yes, sir.

asr-003037
02:46:12.280 --> 02:46:13.740
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Kaya nga, that's my question to you.

asr-003038
02:46:14.440 --> 02:46:15.720
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Ano, which part of it?

asr-003039
02:46:15.960 --> 02:46:17.300
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Is it safety?

asr-003040
02:46:18.040 --> 02:46:20.180
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Is it mura, the economy

asr-003041
02:46:20.180 --> 02:46:21.660
Senator Erwin Tulfo: that their money's worth?

asr-003042
02:46:22.040 --> 02:46:24.220
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Is it tourism?

asr-003043
02:46:24.540 --> 02:46:26.300
Senator Erwin Tulfo: I mean, good surroundings?

asr-003044
02:46:26.540 --> 02:46:27.500
Senator Erwin Tulfo: What is it?

asr-003045
02:46:27.780 --> 02:46:29.180
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: The number one criterion

asr-003046
02:46:29.180 --> 02:46:30.040
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: that they consider

asr-003047
02:46:30.040 --> 02:46:31.380
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: is the cost of living.

asr-003048
02:46:32.140 --> 02:46:33.420
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: That's number one, cost of living.

asr-003049
02:46:33.560 --> 02:46:35.400
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: The second factor is hospitality.

asr-003050
02:46:36.060 --> 02:46:38.020
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: Our people's welcoming attitude.

asr-003051
02:46:38.220 --> 02:46:38.860
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: They like that.

asr-003052
02:46:39.320 --> 02:46:41.440
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: And the fact that we speak English

asr-003053
02:46:41.440 --> 02:46:44.840
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: is also a very important factor for them.

asr-003054
02:46:45.300 --> 02:46:46.820
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: And all the others follow.

asr-003055
02:46:47.520 --> 02:46:47.920
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Okay.

asr-003056
02:46:48.420 --> 02:46:51.220
Senator Erwin Tulfo: My last question for you, sir.

asr-003057
02:46:51.220 --> 02:46:51.520
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: Yes, sir.

asr-003058
02:46:51.520 --> 02:46:56.880
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Is that in light of the Alice Guo case,

asr-003059
02:46:57.780 --> 02:47:00.020
Senator Erwin Tulfo: broader concerns it raised regarding the entry

asr-003060
02:47:00.020 --> 02:47:02.880
Senator Erwin Tulfo: and presence of foreign nationals in the Philippines,

asr-003061
02:47:03.380 --> 02:47:06.820
Senator Erwin Tulfo: how do you monitor that these people are really legit?

asr-003062
02:47:07.480 --> 02:47:08.680
Senator Erwin Tulfo: They're really retirees

asr-003063
02:47:08.680 --> 02:47:13.380
Senator Erwin Tulfo: or probably they're just spies from other countries, sir.

asr-003064
02:47:13.380 --> 02:47:16.020
Senator Erwin Tulfo: And how would you monitor that?

asr-003065
02:47:16.020 --> 02:47:23.380
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Na hindi na tayo napapasok dito ng mga ikang spies

asr-003066
02:47:23.380 --> 02:47:24.500
Senator Erwin Tulfo: in this country?

asr-003067
02:47:24.500 --> 02:47:27.460
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Kasi binabaan pa natin yung retirement age.

asr-003068
02:47:27.780 --> 02:47:28.280
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: Yeah.

asr-003069
02:47:28.280 --> 02:47:28.780
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Go ahead.

asr-003070
02:47:29.780 --> 02:47:33.080
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: First of all, before the monitoring system comes in,

asr-003071
02:47:33.080 --> 02:47:35.780
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: the vetting process,

asr-003072
02:47:35.780 --> 02:47:38.280
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: we improved the security measures

asr-003073
02:47:38.280 --> 02:47:40.980
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: that we impose on these applicants,

asr-003074
02:47:40.980 --> 02:47:44.180
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: especially for the PROC Chinese.

asr-003075
02:47:44.180 --> 02:47:50.080
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: And we improve them by adding additional security measure.

asr-003076
02:47:50.080 --> 02:47:50.880
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: For example,

asr-003077
02:47:50.880 --> 02:47:56.380
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: we hired our own military intelligence officer

asr-003078
02:47:56.380 --> 02:47:57.680
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: as our security.

asr-003079
02:47:57.780 --> 02:47:58.780
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: Officer.

asr-003080
02:47:58.780 --> 02:48:04.280
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: And he interviews all applicants face to face.

asr-003081
02:48:04.280 --> 02:48:06.280
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: If cannot, it can be via Zoom.

asr-003082
02:48:06.280 --> 02:48:09.280
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: But there's always a visual contact.

asr-003083
02:48:09.280 --> 02:48:15.280
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: And this, the other thing that we did is many years ago

asr-003084
02:48:15.280 --> 02:48:19.280
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: when these applicants, especially the Chinese,

asr-003085
02:48:19.280 --> 02:48:21.600
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: they brought in their own interpreters.

asr-003086
02:48:21.720 --> 02:48:24.520
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: So what we did, we hired our own interpreter

asr-003087
02:48:24.520 --> 02:48:26.060
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: so that

asr-003088
02:48:26.060 --> 02:48:27.480
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: you can get what

asr-003089
02:48:27.480 --> 02:48:29.460
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: the red flags are during the conversation.

asr-003090
02:48:29.820 --> 02:48:32.260
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: So all these additional features, sir,

asr-003091
02:48:32.360 --> 02:48:39.080
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: we presented it before we could implement everything.

asr-003092
02:48:39.080 --> 02:48:43.080
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: We presented the whole list of additional security measures

asr-003093
02:48:43.080 --> 02:48:46.080
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: to former Secretary A?o of the NSC.

asr-003094
02:48:46.080 --> 02:48:49.080
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: And he went over it and he approved of it.

asr-003095
02:48:49.080 --> 02:48:51.080
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: And what I told him is,

asr-003096
02:48:51.080 --> 02:48:53.580
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: if you could please write down your approval.

asr-003097
02:48:53.580 --> 02:48:57.580
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: So he issued us a letter saying that it's enough.

asr-003098
02:48:57.580 --> 02:48:59.080
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: The monitoring aspect,

asr-003099
02:48:59.080 --> 02:49:04.580
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: the moment we come, we admit these additional applicants

asr-003100
02:49:04.580 --> 02:49:07.580
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: and we approve their retirement visas,

asr-003101
02:49:07.580 --> 02:49:11.080
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: we send their information to NICA every week.

asr-003102
02:49:11.080 --> 02:49:16.080
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: A list of new retirees that have availed of our retirement visa

asr-003103
02:49:16.080 --> 02:49:19.080
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: is given to NICA for monitoring.

asr-003104
02:49:19.080 --> 02:49:21.080
Senator Erwin Tulfo: How do they, how do you check their backgrounds?

asr-003105
02:49:21.080 --> 02:49:24.580
Senator Erwin Tulfo: I mean, you can only check their backgrounds

asr-003106
02:49:24.580 --> 02:49:26.580
Senator Erwin Tulfo: when they're already here or

asr-003107
02:49:27.580 --> 02:49:29.080
Senator Erwin Tulfo: or kahit na nandoon pa sila in another country,

asr-003108
02:49:29.080 --> 02:49:30.580
Senator Erwin Tulfo: in their own country.

asr-003109
02:49:30.580 --> 02:49:32.580
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Is there a way to check it?

asr-003110
02:49:32.580 --> 02:49:35.580
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Baka mamaya ito ay pedophile, itong retiree na ito.

asr-003111
02:49:35.580 --> 02:49:39.580
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Itong retiree na ito ay may kasong murder.

asr-003112
02:49:39.580 --> 02:49:44.080
Senator Erwin Tulfo: And then just want to retire or running away from their own laws.

asr-003113
02:49:44.080 --> 02:49:46.080
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Baka wanted po yun.

asr-003114
02:49:46.080 --> 02:49:48.080
Senator Erwin Tulfo: So how do you do that?

asr-003115
02:49:48.080 --> 02:49:49.080
Senator Erwin Tulfo: How do you check?

asr-003116
02:49:49.080 --> 02:49:55.080
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: What we do, sir, is we have access to the Interpol database.

asr-003117
02:49:55.080 --> 02:49:57.580
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: So we can check every applicant.

asr-003118
02:49:57.580 --> 02:50:00.580
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: Aside from that, we require each applicant

asr-003119
02:50:00.580 --> 02:50:04.580
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: to present to us a police clearance from their country of origin

asr-003120
02:50:04.580 --> 02:50:06.580
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: and it must be apostilled

asr-003121
02:50:06.580 --> 02:50:09.580
PRA General Manager and CEO Roberto Z. Zozobrado: to be sure that it's factual and correct.

asr-003122
02:50:09.580 --> 02:50:13.580
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Alright, thank you, sir. Thank you, Mr. Sosobrado.

asr-003123
02:50:13.580 --> 02:50:15.580
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Let me go to Yusec Azurin.

asr-003124
02:50:15.580 --> 02:50:18.580
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Sir, anong ginagawa ninyo or what have you done?

asr-003125
02:50:18.580 --> 02:50:22.580
Senator Erwin Tulfo: May adjustments? Itong pong mga Israeli sa Siargao,

asr-003126
02:50:22.580 --> 02:50:24.580
Senator Erwin Tulfo: natapos na po ba yan?

asr-003127
02:50:24.580 --> 02:50:27.580
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Yung mga, yung holdapan po sa

asr-003128
02:50:27.580 --> 02:50:29.580
Senator Erwin Tulfo: El Nido.

asr-003129
02:50:29.580 --> 02:50:31.580
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Dabagamat hindi naman foreigners ang in-hold up,

asr-003130
02:50:31.580 --> 02:50:34.580
Senator Erwin Tulfo: kundi mga local community stores po doon.

asr-003131
02:50:34.580 --> 02:50:37.580
Senator Erwin Tulfo: How do you step up yung security of our tourists?

asr-003132
02:50:37.580 --> 02:50:41.580
Senator Erwin Tulfo: This is one of the reasons why medyo nagdadalawang isip sila.

asr-003133
02:50:41.580 --> 02:50:45.580
Senator Erwin Tulfo: I'd rather go to Vietnam kasi medyo tahimik.

asr-003134
02:50:45.580 --> 02:50:49.580
Senator Erwin Tulfo: I'd rather go, sasabihin, I'd rather go to Thailand, medyo safe doon.

asr-003135
02:50:49.580 --> 02:50:53.580
Senator Erwin Tulfo: So how, how, what are you doing right now?

asr-003136
02:50:53.580 --> 02:50:54.580
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Or what can be done?

asr-003137
02:50:54.580 --> 02:50:56.580
Senator Erwin Tulfo: I mean, may nakikita akong tourist police,

asr-003138
02:50:56.580 --> 02:50:58.580
Senator Erwin Tulfo: pero sa umaga lang.

asr-003139
02:50:58.580 --> 02:51:04.580
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Sa gabi, when I go around sa mga island tourist destinations,

asr-003140
02:51:04.580 --> 02:51:07.580
Senator Erwin Tulfo: parang nawawala na yung police natin sa umaga lang.

asr-003141
02:51:07.580 --> 02:51:11.580
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Or dito sa Metro Manila, nakikita ko sa gabi, palakad-lakad sila.

asr-003142
02:51:11.580 --> 02:51:17.580
Senator Erwin Tulfo: So anong adjustments ang ginagawa po ng DOT pertaining to this, to the safety?

asr-003143
02:51:17.580 --> 02:51:19.580
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Kasi yung pang-una magiging concern eh.

asr-003144
02:51:19.580 --> 02:51:22.580
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Will I, shall I bring my family to the Philippines?

asr-003145
02:51:22.580 --> 02:51:24.580
Senator Erwin Tulfo: My wife and my two kids?

asr-003146
02:51:24.580 --> 02:51:28.580
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Will it be safe if we go around the streets at night?

asr-003147
02:51:28.580 --> 02:51:33.580
Senator Erwin Tulfo: In Boracay, in El Nido, in wherever?

asr-003148
02:51:33.580 --> 02:51:35.580
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Will it be safe?

asr-003149
02:51:35.580 --> 02:51:40.580
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Ano ang programa nyo rito, Yusek Azurin?

asr-003150
02:51:40.580 --> 02:51:42.580
DOT Undersecretary Rodolfo Azurin Jr.: Thank you, Mr. Chair, sir.

asr-003151
02:51:42.580 --> 02:51:43.580
DOT Undersecretary Rodolfo Azurin Jr.: Good evening po.

asr-003152
02:51:43.580 --> 02:51:51.580
DOT Undersecretary Rodolfo Azurin Jr.: I think, sir, one of the programs that we are pushing with the Department of Tourism right now is

asr-003153
02:51:51.580 --> 02:51:54.580
DOT Undersecretary Rodolfo Azurin Jr.: to coordinate with the security sector.

asr-003154
02:51:54.580 --> 02:52:00.580
DOT Undersecretary Rodolfo Azurin Jr.: The Philippine National Police, the Armed Forces of the Philippines and the Philippine Coast Guard

asr-003155
02:52:00.580 --> 02:52:07.580
DOT Undersecretary Rodolfo Azurin Jr.: because they are a factor, sir, in keeping our country safe and secure.

asr-003156
02:52:07.580 --> 02:52:12.580
DOT Undersecretary Rodolfo Azurin Jr.: And as a matter of fact, with respect to the problem in Siargao,

asr-003157
02:52:12.580 --> 02:52:17.580
DOT Undersecretary Rodolfo Azurin Jr.: more or less, sir, mayroon tayong 500 na Israeli doon.

asr-003158
02:52:17.580 --> 02:52:22.580
DOT Undersecretary Rodolfo Azurin Jr.: And sometimes, yung report kasi, sir, masyadong na-hype.

asr-003159
02:52:22.580 --> 02:52:24.580
DOT Undersecretary Rodolfo Azurin Jr.: But for this year alone,

asr-003160
02:52:24.580 --> 02:52:31.580
DOT Undersecretary Rodolfo Azurin Jr.: there are only about eight na cases against the Israelis

asr-003161
02:52:31.580 --> 02:52:38.580
DOT Undersecretary Rodolfo Azurin Jr.: na they committed against other foreign visitors and sa mga locals po.

asr-003162
02:52:38.580 --> 02:52:42.580
DOT Undersecretary Rodolfo Azurin Jr.: And these cases are already solved, sir.

asr-003163
02:52:42.580 --> 02:52:51.580
DOT Undersecretary Rodolfo Azurin Jr.: Karamihan po ng kaso, sir, ay yung reckless imprudence resulting to damage to property or physical injury.

asr-003164
02:52:51.580 --> 02:52:53.580
DOT Undersecretary Rodolfo Azurin Jr.: And lately, sir,

asr-003165
02:52:53.580 --> 02:52:55.580
DOT Undersecretary Rodolfo Azurin Jr.: we coordinated with the Philippine National Police

asr-003166
02:52:55.580 --> 02:53:03.580
DOT Undersecretary Rodolfo Azurin Jr.: because the DOT does not have any database on the crimes

asr-003167
02:53:03.580 --> 02:53:07.580
DOT Undersecretary Rodolfo Azurin Jr.: that are being committed against our foreign tourists for the last five years.

asr-003168
02:53:07.580 --> 02:53:13.580
DOT Undersecretary Rodolfo Azurin Jr.: And we were able, sir, to get from the IDM of the Philippine National Police.

asr-003169
02:53:13.580 --> 02:53:21.580
DOT Undersecretary Rodolfo Azurin Jr.: And out of the 9,000, sir, na cases from 2022 to date, sir,

asr-003170
02:53:21.580 --> 02:53:26.580
DOT Undersecretary Rodolfo Azurin Jr.: more than 50 percent po, sir, ay it's more on safety issues.

asr-003171
02:53:26.580 --> 02:53:33.580
DOT Undersecretary Rodolfo Azurin Jr.: Like, sabi ko nga, sir, is reckless imprudence resulting to damage to property,

asr-003172
02:53:33.580 --> 02:53:41.580
DOT Undersecretary Rodolfo Azurin Jr.: reckless imprudence resulting to damage that cause injury,

asr-003173
02:53:41.580 --> 02:53:44.580
DOT Undersecretary Rodolfo Azurin Jr.: or sometimes, sir, homicide.

asr-003174
02:53:44.580 --> 02:53:49.580
DOT Undersecretary Rodolfo Azurin Jr.: For the theft and robbery, sir, kukunti-kunti lamang po yun, sir.

asr-003175
02:53:49.580 --> 02:53:53.580
DOT Undersecretary Rodolfo Azurin Jr.: Ang ginagawa po natin ngayon is we are trying to separate

asr-003176
02:53:53.580 --> 02:53:59.580
DOT Undersecretary Rodolfo Azurin Jr.: what are the security issues and what are the safety issues

asr-003177
02:53:59.580 --> 02:54:03.580
DOT Undersecretary Rodolfo Azurin Jr.: so that when we present, kasi, sir, ang PNP, AFP, and Coast Guard,

asr-003178
02:54:03.580 --> 02:54:07.580
DOT Undersecretary Rodolfo Azurin Jr.: hindi naman silang humaharap, sir, sa mga embassies and sa DFA.

asr-003179
02:54:07.580 --> 02:54:09.580
DOT Undersecretary Rodolfo Azurin Jr.: It's the DOT or the DFA.

asr-003180
02:54:09.580 --> 02:54:15.580
DOT Undersecretary Rodolfo Azurin Jr.: That's why when the embassy issues a travel advisory na medyo negative, sir,

asr-003181
02:54:15.580 --> 02:54:17.580
DOT Undersecretary Rodolfo Azurin Jr.: hindi po natin na nasasagot agad.

asr-003182
02:54:17.580 --> 02:54:18.580
DOT Undersecretary Rodolfo Azurin Jr.: Now, sir,

asr-003183
02:54:18.580 --> 02:54:23.580
DOT Undersecretary Rodolfo Azurin Jr.: we are trying to formulate our own database

asr-003184
02:54:23.580 --> 02:54:27.580
DOT Undersecretary Rodolfo Azurin Jr.: so that we can brief any embassies, sir,

asr-003185
02:54:27.580 --> 02:54:31.580
DOT Undersecretary Rodolfo Azurin Jr.: with respect sa mga travel advisories, sir, na ini-issue po nila, sir.

asr-003186
02:54:31.580 --> 02:54:35.580
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Have you or are you looking into this?

asr-003187
02:54:35.580 --> 02:54:37.580
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Sa TripAdvisor po,

asr-003188
02:54:37.580 --> 02:54:41.580
Senator Erwin Tulfo: pag tinype mo Intramuros, nakalagay po doon scam.

asr-003189
02:54:41.580 --> 02:54:44.580
Senator Erwin Tulfo: How are we going to resolve that?

asr-003190
02:54:44.580 --> 02:54:47.580
Senator Erwin Tulfo: So kung ako ang turista, hindi pa ako nakapunta sa Intramuros,

asr-003191
02:54:47.580 --> 02:54:49.580
Senator Erwin Tulfo: narinig ko lang sa office mate ko,

asr-003192
02:54:49.580 --> 02:54:51.580
Senator Erwin Tulfo: ah, it's beautiful there.

asr-003193
02:54:51.580 --> 02:54:54.580
Senator Erwin Tulfo: So na-type ko, diba, alam mo naman yung mga foreigner.

asr-003194
02:54:54.580 --> 02:54:56.580
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Intramuros.

asr-003195
02:54:56.580 --> 02:54:58.580
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Lalabas po doon mga scam.

asr-003196
02:54:58.580 --> 02:55:02.580
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Na-scam sila sa tricycle, na-scam sila sa kalesa,

asr-003197
02:55:02.580 --> 02:55:04.580
Senator Erwin Tulfo: overcharge sila, etc.

asr-003198
02:55:04.580 --> 02:55:06.580
Senator Erwin Tulfo: Mate-turn off ako,

asr-003199
02:55:06.580 --> 02:55:11.580
Senator Erwin Tulfo: how are we addressing this issue na itong mga scam na ito na,

asr-003200
02:55:11.580 --> 02:55:14.580
Senator Erwin Tulfo: sa lahat pa naman ng lugar, itong Intramuros pa?

asr-003201
02:55:14.580 --> 02:55:15.580
DOT Undersecretary Rodolfo Azurin Jr.: Yes, sir.

asr-003202
02:55:15.580 --> 02:55:16.580
DOT Undersecretary Rodolfo Azurin Jr.: Actually, sir, ito nga ho, sir, yung...

asr-003203
02:55:17.580 --> 02:55:19.580
DOT Undersecretary Rodolfo Azurin Jr.: problema na nakikita natin, sir,

asr-003204
02:55:19.580 --> 02:55:24.580
DOT Undersecretary Rodolfo Azurin Jr.: marami hong issues na hindi ho issue ng DOT

asr-003205
02:55:24.580 --> 02:55:26.580
DOT Undersecretary Rodolfo Azurin Jr.: but concern ho ng DOT because

asr-003206
02:55:26.580 --> 02:55:30.580
DOT Undersecretary Rodolfo Azurin Jr.: it affects really yung tourism industry natin, sir.

asr-003207
02:55:30.580 --> 02:55:33.580
DOT Undersecretary Rodolfo Azurin Jr.: Because it's the DOT who promotes our country

asr-003208
02:55:33.580 --> 02:55:36.580
DOT Undersecretary Rodolfo Azurin Jr.: to local and foreign visitors po, sir.

asr-003209
02:55:36.580 --> 02:55:40.580
DOT Undersecretary Rodolfo Azurin Jr.: And we are proposing, sir, that

asr-003210
02:55:40.580 --> 02:55:44.580
DOT Undersecretary Rodolfo Azurin Jr.: the Secretary of Tourism, sir,

asr-003211
02:55:44.580 --> 02:55:48.580
DOT Undersecretary Rodolfo Azurin Jr.: will be the head of council, sir,

asr-003212
02:55:48.580 --> 02:55:52.580
DOT Undersecretary Rodolfo Azurin Jr.: National Tourism for Safety and Security Council.

asr-003213
02:55:52.580 --> 02:55:58.580
DOT Undersecretary Rodolfo Azurin Jr.: Kaya, sir, meron mga certain mga issues, sir, na

asr-003214
02:55:58.580 --> 02:56:02.580
DOT Undersecretary Rodolfo Azurin Jr.: we need the cooperation of the LGU, sir.

asr-003215
02:56:02.580 --> 02:56:08.580
DOT Undersecretary Rodolfo Azurin Jr.: And so far, sir, hindi ho lahat ng LGU ay nagkukumplay po ng mga requirement ng DOT.

asr-003216
02:56:08.580 --> 02:56:12.580
DOT Undersecretary Rodolfo Azurin Jr.: Like, for example, sir, the accreditation po, sir.

asr-003217
02:56:12.580 --> 02:56:16.580
DOT Undersecretary Rodolfo Azurin Jr.: Hindi ho lahat ay nagpapa-accredit sa DOT.

asr-003218
02:56:16.580 --> 02:56:19.580
DOT Undersecretary Rodolfo Azurin Jr.: For example, sir, yun hong nangyaring

asr-003219
02:56:19.580 --> 02:56:23.580
DOT Undersecretary Rodolfo Azurin Jr.: aksidente sa Aurora na may nalunod na Nigerian

asr-003220
02:56:23.580 --> 02:56:26.580
DOT Undersecretary Rodolfo Azurin Jr.: and a basketballista, sir, sa Ateneo,

asr-003221
02:56:26.580 --> 02:56:29.580
DOT Undersecretary Rodolfo Azurin Jr.: yun pong resort na pinuntahan doon, sir,

asr-003222
02:56:29.580 --> 02:56:33.580
DOT Undersecretary Rodolfo Azurin Jr.: ay hindi ho accredited ng DOT.

asr-003223
02:56:33.580 --> 02:56:36.580
DOT Undersecretary Rodolfo Azurin Jr.: So, saan po natin ipipinpoint yung accountability?

asr-003224
02:56:36.580 --> 02:56:41.580
DOT Undersecretary Rodolfo Azurin Jr.: Is it yung LGU na nag-issue ng business permit?

asr-003225
